NTkwODMwMjU2MTI4",__typename:"NoteTweetResults",result:$R[202]={__ref:"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNjI5MTc1OTA4MzAyNTYxMjg="},id:"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0UmVzdWx0czoyMDYyOTE3NTkwODMwMjU2MTI4"},"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNjI5MTc1OTA4MzAyNTYxMjg=":$R[203]={__id:"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNjI5MTc1OTA4MzAyNTYxMjg=",__typename:"NoteTweet",text:"Day 3 closed out Fin Labs New York on a high note.\n\nPaul Adams, CPO at Fin, opened the day with an executive briefing that set the context for everything that followed.\n\nThen Dee Kapila, Rati Zvirawa, and Angel Horowitz from DaySmart led a fireside on where AI agents actually stand today, and what it takes for teams still on the sidelines to make their move.\n\nNext, Rigby Crawford, Santiago Luque, and Eric Broulette from Bloomerang walked through what great Fin deployment looks like in practice, with real examples from real teams.\n\nThen Brian Donohue closed the event with Prithvi Rajasekaran from Anthropic, telling the story of how doubling engineering productivity with AI unlocked something bigger: a full product rebuild and a new baseline for what a modern product team can ship.\n\nThree days in midtown. Hundreds of leaders and practitioners who showed up ready to build.\n\nThank you to everyone who joined us and made Fin Labs New York what it was. We're just getting started.",entity_set:$R[204]={__ref:"client:Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNjI5MTc1OTA4MzAyNTYxMjg=:entity_set"},id:"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNjI5MTc1OTA4MzAyNTYxMjg="},"client:Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNjI5MTc1OTA4MzAyNTYxMjg=:entity_set":$R[205]={__id:"client:Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNjI5MTc1OTA4MzAyNTYxMjg=:entity_set",__typename:"EntitySet",hashtags:$R[206]={__refs:$R[207]=[]},symbols:$R[208]={__refs:$R[209]=[]},smarttags:$R[210]={__refs:$R[211]=[]},urls:$R[212]={__refs:$R[213]=[]},user_mentions:$R[214]={__refs:$R[215]=[]}},"client:VHdlZXQ6MjA2MjkxNzU5MDk2NDM5MjA2Mg==:grok_translated_post_with_availability":$R[216]={__id:"client:VHdlZXQ6MjA2MjkxNzU5MDk2NDM5MjA2Mg==:grok_translated_post_with_availability",__typename:"ApiGrokTranslateResponse